# Fixture: llama.cpp server output, documented format.

This is a log in the format llama.cpp's `llama-server` emits, used to test the
`measure` path. It is written from the documented output format rather than
captured on this machine: the build host is Apple Silicon with no CUDA or ROCm
stack, and no llama.cpp log existed on disk to capture. Where a real log would
differ, it would differ in values, not in structure.

The two-device section reproduces the imbalance from evidence #1 of
work order prod-20260929-002: the model buffers differ by roughly 1.4 GiB with
`--tensor-split 0.667,0.333`, so the tool has a real example to report on.

